cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this methodology or software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ADS-Cascade"
abstract: >-
  A data-driven method for deciding how much of a classification problem
  actually needs a model. An Automated Determinism Score (ADS) is computed
  per item before any classifier is built, and a four-tier confidence
  cascade uses an LLM only as a re-ranker over retrieved candidates for the
  measured minority tail. Validated end to end on Romanian fiscal-document
  classification (D406/SAF-T invoices and photographed retail receipts);
  the method itself is not specific to that domain.
authors:
